quired repair: a fresh attempt is accepted ONLY from states where no effect is known to have been\napplied - `INTENDED` and `UNKNOWN_EFFECT`. From `PARTIAL_EFFECT`, `OBSERVED`, `READBACK`, `DENIED`,\n`RECONCILED`, `IRREVERSIBLE` a fresh attempt is REFUSED with a typed error and a specific\n`reason_code` (`FRESH_ATTEMPT_REFUSED_PARTIAL_EFFECT` for the partial case). Duplicate-key detection\nmust still fire first. `README.md` and the docstrings must state the same rule. Add tests: partial ->\nrefused; unknown_effect -> accepted; duplicate key -> duplicate error; and the accepted path still\nreaches `RECONCILED` through observe/readback/reconcile.\n\n## F2 — `src/effect/idempotency.py`: retry allowed from mid-flight states\n\n`plan_retry`/`assert_retryable` currently allow `ATTEMPTED`/`OBSERVED`/`READBACK`, contradicting the\nmodule's own statement that a retry is allowed ONLY from `UNKNOWN_EFFECT`.\n\nRequired repair: `RETRYABLE_STATES = (\"UNKNOWN_EFFECT\",)`. A mid-flight record is refused with\n`reason_code=\"RETRY_REFUSED_MID_FLIGHT\"` (and `RetryRefused` from `assert_retryable`); the documented\npath for a mid-flight record is `finalize()` (which normalises it to `UNKNOWN_EFFECT`) and then a\nretry, or a re-observe. Keep the UNKNOWN_EFFECT retry working end-to-end and keep the existing\nrefusals for RECONCILED / DENIED / IRREVERSIBLE / PARTIAL_EFFECT. Add tests for each.\n\n## F3 — `src/observability/redaction.py`: the receipt hides what it destroyed\n\n`redact_event` replaces unscannable bytes with a marker but reports `safe=True` and drops the count.\n\nRequired repair: the receipt must carry `unscannable_bytes: N` and `safe` must be `False` whenever\nanything was replaced that could not be scanned; the module docstring must say that unscannable values\nare destroyed. Add tests: a payload with benign bytes -> `unscannable_bytes >= 1` and `safe is False`;\na payload with no unscannable value and no secret -> `safe is True` with `unscannable_bytes == 0`.\n\n## F4