n\n## F6 — `src/assurance/oracle.py`: the negative-fixture manifest is under-constrained\n\nA reviewer passed `negative_fixture_manifest={'NEG-X': 'TEST_RUN'}` (a kind already required by the\nplan) or `{'NEG-X': 'NEG-X'}` (the fixture's own name) and the oracle PASSED with no dedicated proof.\n\nRequired repair: the bound kind must be a DEDICATED negative-fixture proof kind: it must not equal the\nfixture id and must not be one of the plan's `required_evidence_kinds`. A manifest that violates this\nis not a representation; report `reason_code=\"NEGATIVE_FIXTURE_MANIFEST_UNCONSTRAINED\"` and treat the\nfixture as unreprsented (fail closed). A genuine manifest binding the fixture to a dedicated,\npresent, non-required kind still PASSES. Add tests for all three cases plus the round-3 regression\ncases (absent kind, empty manifest, substring item_id, mis-nested manifest).\n\n## Definition of done\n\nAll four affected roots must pass with counts strictly GREATER than 183 / 105 / 128 / 97:\n\n```\npython -m unittest discover -s src/security/tests      -t src/security/tests\npython -m unittest discover -s src/effect/tests        -t src/effect/tests\npython -m unittest discover -s src/assurance/tests     -t src/assurance/tests\npython -m unittest discover -s src/observability/tests -t src/observability/tests\n```\n\nPrint a JSON object when finished:\n`{\"files\": [...], \"counts\": {\"security\": N, \"effect\": N, \"assurance\": N, \"observability\": N}}`.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
